  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Flood Affected Populations in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burundi continues to be affected by climate-induced hazards which exacerbate existing socioeconomic vulnerabilities and heighten humanitarian needs. It is also located in an earthquake-prone geographic zone of the African Great Lakes, increasing exposure to catastrophic events. In recent years, disasters from frequent floods and storms have provoked massive displacement of persons, and at an increasing rate; dangerous storms involving violent winds and torrential rains have also caused severe damage to property and populations. This project is supporting the efforts of the Government of Burundi through a multisectoral approach response to internal displacement triggered by natural hazards by ensuring that affected populations have improved living conditions through shelter, non-food items, water, sanitation and hygiene and health assistance; and affected and vulnerable populations have improved protection and mental health and psychosocial wellbeing through evidence-based humanitarian assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
